-- the problem, stated (Avik, 2026-11-18: "CAN YOU EVEN STATE THE PROBLEM FORMALLY THAT YOU'RE TRYING TO
-- SOLVE?"). C is the type of configurations: X(s), the chain's atoms placed in space up to proper motion,
-- when coordinates are written, and any type until then. A fold problem is what physics fixes for a
-- chain s under conditions κ: the configurations that keep the chain's arrangements (X_L(s), where every
-- sign of every stereocentre is the one its Cyc gives), the metastable basins of the dynamics of the
-- Coulomb Hamiltonian of G(s) in κ, which configurations lie in which basin, and the rates between
-- basins. No constant in it is chosen; the only numbers in the Hamiltonian are physical constants.
-- Anfinsen's result is that this is a function of (s, κ); the problem is to compute it.
FoldProblem : Type 0 → Type 1
FoldProblem C = (L : C → Type 0) × (B : Type 0) × (B → C → Type 0) × Interconv B
